{
  "name": "Track daily habits and mood with Telegram buttons, Google Sheets and a weekly Gemini review",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track daily habits and mood with Telegram buttons, Google Sheets and a weekly Gemini review\n\nA habit tracker you never have to open. Every evening your Telegram bot asks how your day was (mood 1-5) and sends one question per habit with **Done** and **Not today** buttons. Taps are saved to Google Sheets, `/stats` shows your last 7 days with streaks, and every Sunday Gemini writes a short, kind review with one small experiment for next week.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every evening at 9pm** sends the mood question, reads your `Habits` tab and sends one button message per active habit.\n2. **Receive Telegram update** gets button presses and messages. **Parse the update** decodes each button into a log row with a key `date|habit_id`, so pressing again simply changes the answer.\n3. Answers are upserted into the `Log` tab, the button is acknowledged and the message is edited to show what you chose.\n4. `/stats` reads both tabs and replies with done counts, completion % and current streaks.\n5. **Every Sunday at 7pm** calculates the week, including mood on days you did a habit versus days you did not, and Gemini turns it into a short review.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a bot with @BotFather; add **Telegram**, **Google Sheets** and **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credentials.\n2. Create a sheet with `Habits` (`habit_id, habit, emoji, active, target_per_week`) and `Log` (`log_id, date, habit_id, value, logged_at`) tabs.\n3. Each trigger has its own settings node: put the Sheet ID and your chat ID in **Set tracker settings**, **Config** and **Config (Every Sunday at 7pm)**. Activate.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the check-in time, or add habits as new rows; no workflow edits needed.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 600
      },
